From: Armin <2369138+Arminova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:26:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Flash Next CUDA: prompt rows in the prompt form whatever
 the pass size

A prompt's bits depended on how many rows its pass had: the MXFP8 prompt tile (from 256 rows), bf16 MoE slots
(from the expert prompt tile's 64 rows) and the fused FMA DeltaNet chain (from 64 rows) applied to large lone
passes only. Every place that splits a fill moved rows across those lines: with the prompt cache on, a kept
state at a block boundary split a 1,071-token prompt into 1,064 rows and a 7-row tail, and the replies changed.

Hooks.prompt (set by every fill: the lanes' fill and the drafted prefillChunk) now chooses by what the rows are:
- prompt rows take the MXFP8 / BF16 prompt tile and the fused up-mix at any size (Kernels.nativeMatmul and
  tiles.matmul take `prompt`; the tile's per-row arithmetic does not depend on m)
- bf16 MoE slots key on prompt rows alone; short passes stay on the decode expert tiles, whose bf16 epilogue
  (EPI 3) is the prompt tiles' on the same sums
- the fused DeltaNet chain takes every prompt pass
Other lone passes keep the row rules; two ranks keep them too (the second rank's hooks carry only the logits).

GB10, FP4-Local: greedy and seeded-sampled reply hashes on 300- to 15,000-token prompts are equal with the
prompt cache on (4 resumed prompts) and off, bf16 and FP8 KV; with the cache off they equal the build before.
Speed unchanged (mixed 4 streams 123.0 tok/s, prompts 2,282 / 2,292 at 4K / 16K); tasks 123 / 130.
